Package: call-ducker
Architecture: any
# pipewire-pulse does not declare Provides: pulseaudio, so the alternation has to
# be explicit. PipeWire comes first because it is the default on both Debian 13
# and Ubuntu 24.04; naming pulseaudio first would pull the legacy server onto a
# system that already has a working pipewire-pulse.
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         pipewire-pulse | pulseaudio
Description: Adjust game audio automatically during calls
 CallDucker sets background applications to a chosen absolute volume while a
 voice call is active, then restores every stream to its original per-channel
 volume, including its channel layout.
 .
 It works with a native PulseAudio server and with PipeWire's pipewire-pulse
 compatibility server. The daemon runs as a systemd user service and talks to
 libpulse directly; it does not access the network, collect telemetry, or
 require a root service.
